# Board + move join (keep it useful)

**Intent:** the policy must still be able to bind a legal row to what is on the
pitch (dest square, lanes, defenders). Do **not** quietly replace that with a
lossy summary that makes the join useless.

**Not the intent:** a permanent ban on attention or any pooling. Named
alternatives (e.g. move→board cross-attn over the full token grid) are fine when
chosen explicitly — say so in the change / docs; do not sneak them in as “still
full board.”

## Live default (until replaced on purpose)

```
pitch CNN → map (N, C, H, W) → flatten
non-pitch (benches / scalars / …) kept as-is
row_emb = encode_legal_rows(full pack)
row_scorer([ flatten(map) ‖ non_pitch ‖ row_emb ])
```

Value head may still GAP the pitch into the SB3 `features_dim` vector — that is
for the critic / stock extractor contract, **not** a substitute for the join.

## Do not

- Ship **GAP-only**, **endpoint-only**, or other joins that throw away the map
  without an explicit product reason in the PR / chat
- Defend “a global vibe / one gathered cell is enough” when the ask is board × move
- Silently swap the live join for a thinner readout and leave docs/rules claiming
  flatten-full-map

## Do

- Flag in chat when this rule would block a **named** design (cross-attn, etc.)
  — ask rather than veto on autopilot
- Keep the full legal-row encoding on the score path (no row stub / kind-only score)

See [`ai/PPO_STRATEGY.md`](ai/PPO_STRATEGY.md) (stock vs deviations; flatten cost).
